  "meaningBoundary": "Both finite scalar and FMA expression paths, their range predicates, referenced constants and shared CRT table/selector joins are authenticated against the selected native triplet. The normal output preserves instruction order rather than substituting mathematical exp. Partial named CRT expf/expf_sse2 code and exact named-table correspondence support family identity; the shipped merged method differs. Special paths select zero, infinity or quieted input-NaN candidates. NaN flag one bypasses the external error routine; finite underflow/overflow flags two/three call it, retaining the candidate under callee-saved ABI preservation. Runtime selector initialization, error/errno callbacks, trap behavior, nondefault MXCSR, arbitrary-input math equivalence and live DSP invocation remain open."
